<title>POLAND: Poland ups T-bill offer to PLN 4.9 bln in March.</title>
<headline>Poland ups T-bill offer to PLN 4.9 bln in March.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Finance Ministry increased its T-bill offer to 4.9 billion zlotys in March from 4.0 billion in February, it said in a statement on Thursday.  </p>
<p>According to its preliminary plan, which can be changed, the ministry will not offer 39-week paper next month.</p>
<p>TENTATIVE MARCH T-BILL OFFER SCHEDULE (in million zlotys)</p>
<p>		 March 3     March 10     March 17     March 24</p>
<p>   8-week	 400	   400	     0		0</p>
<p>  13-week	 200	   200	   400	    400</p>
<p>  26-week	 200	   200	   200	    200</p>
<p>  52-week	 400	   500	   600	    600</p>
<p>   TOTAL	 1200	  1300	  1200	   1200</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
